    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Bictegravir/tenofovir alafenamide/emtricitabine (one tablet) = a common INSTI-based starting option for most adults."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Coformulated bictegravir = contraindicated w RIF or rifabutin TB tx (they lower its levels and risk ART failure)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Long-acting cabotegravir (INSTI) + rilpivirine (NNRTI): IM inj Q2M, for adults on a stable regimen who are virologically suppressed. Often started orally for 4 wks to check tolerance. Pts w active hepatitis B are often excluded (⍉hepatitis B activity)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Lenacapavir (capsid inhibitor): inj Q6M w an optimized background regimen, for heavily treatment-experienced adults w multidrug resistance."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
